# MemNet under Multitask Mode

**WHEN** Multitask Mode is on, or Task / background sub-agents are active:
open and follow `~/.cursor/skills/memnet-multitask/SKILL.md`.

**ELSE** (single-agent): use the MemNet goldfish loop rule; in-process MCP is OK.
Tools / dialect: `mcp-memnet`, `memnet-format` -- do not re-copy here.

## Transport

- MUST use shared MemNet: TCP `:18765` (`memnet serve`) or streamable-http (`:18766/mcp`).
- MUST NOT use in-process MCP under Multitask (isolated graph per process).
- If serve is down or MemNet tools are absent: skip MemNet; plain Markdown only (no TOON/TRON).

## Parent coordinator

- MUST open or load **one** mission session id; pass it in every worker prompt.
- MUST mint and settle `TSK_*` / `USR_*` from shared-session pin-map facts (not from worker chat).
- MUST end the turn after background spawn -- no poll, no await.
- Next coordinator turn: `pin_map` first; act from the refreshed slice.
- Prefer one worker per coherent workstream; parallel only with disjoint anchors or separate session ids.

## Worker

- MUST use the parent's session id; `pin_map` first every turn.
- MUST mutate only the assigned subgraph; MUST NOT invent ids the parent already minted.
- MUST NOT settle parent-owned `TSK_*` / `USR_*` unless delegated.
- MUST NOT open a different session unless explicitly assigned.

## Scope

House-generic. Projects may pin mission anchors in `AGENT-CONTEXT.md` -- MUST NOT hardcode one repo here.
Chat is never mission SSOT.
